the eight run-admitting strata all lie in the five run-carrying pieces), so each block sum is
divisible by `p^φ̃` TERMWISE through `Zeta2PtpBlock.blockSum_dvd_of_noShort`.  On each stratum
where the six floors are constant, `φ̃ ≤ bitsR p r u` is `omega` after `Zeta2PtpCong`'s
`residue_spec` / `bit*_abstract` rewrites — `bits_S1 … bits_S7`'s proof with the stratum's own
floors.  Per piece: the strata bounds, the φ̃ wire (`Zeta2PtpS7.phiT_of_mem`), and the dispatcher.

`gen_ptp_runfree.py --check` reds if this file drifts from its generator (LEAN.md §10).

